id: pm-vcs-7ydb
title: selfhost.bundle crossed GitHub's 50 MB warning and grows with every commit toward the 100 MB push limit
description: "On 2026-10-12, pushing the close-out branch warned that selfhost.bundle is 50.53 MB, above GitHub's recommended 50 MB maximum. The bundle is regenerated for every commit, including tracker-only commits, and grows with history; at 100 MB GitHub rejects the push outright, which would block every PR and release. Options: an incremental or thin bundle against a recorded base, compressing or pruning objects that are not needed for self-host verification, moving the full bundle to a release asset with only its digest committed, or Git LFS (which needs evaluation against the self-host contract)."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: ci,self-host,size
created_at: "2026-10-12T00:59:40.128Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T00:59:40.816Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "A committed self-host artifact stays well below 50 MB as history grows (measured over a projected year of commits), accept:self-host still proves byte-identity of the committed source, and pushes no longer emit the GitHub large-file warning."
body: ""
